@.str.158 = private unnamed_addr constant [896 x i8] c"Create a triangle mesh from a text string.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    text (str): The text for generating the mesh. ASCII characters 32-126 are\0A        supported (includes alphanumeric characters and punctuation). In\0A        addition the line feed '\\n' is supported to start a new line.\0A    depth (float): The depth of the generated mesh. If depth is 0 then a flat mesh will be generated.\0A    float_dtype (o3d.core.Dtype): Float type for the vertices. Either Float32 or Float64.\0A    int_dtype (o3d.core.Dtype): Int type for the triangle indices. Either Int32 or Int64.\0A    device (o3d.core.Device): The device for the returned mesh.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    Text as triangle mesh.\0A\0AExample:\0A    This shows how to simplify the Stanford Bunny mesh::\0A\0A        import open3d as o3d\0A\0A        mesh = o3d.t.geometry.TriangleMesh.create_text('Open3D', depth=1)\0A        o3d.visualization.draw([{'name': 'text', 'geometry': mesh}])\0A\00", align 1
